A dev database of branch B ran B's step as the ledger's step 2. Branch A
merged first, so after the merge step 2 is A's and B's is step 3: to that
database, its step 2 was edited. Refused rather than skip A's step or run
B's twice; a dev database is remade, or each branch keeps its own
(`ROUX_DATABASE=dev-$(git branch --show-current).db`).

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'Pea Soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;
-- Branch B: notes.
ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN note TEXT;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT, note TEXT) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;
-- Branch A: slugs.
ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN slug TEXT;
-- Branch B: notes.
ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN note TEXT;

== plan
-- after 1
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's steps 1 to 2
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;
  step 2
    ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN note TEXT;
-- after 2

== error
-- after 2
ledger.sql's step 2 is not what the database ran. It ran:
  ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN note TEXT;
ledger.sql says:
  ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN slug TEXT;
A step that ran stays as it is: put it back, and add a step after it. (A database that ran a draft of the step, a dev one: put back the copy made before it, in `<database>.before-ledger/`.)
